From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alejandro Corbellini <acorbellini@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Feb 2026 23:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: fix Miyoo Flip bootargs for Knulli

The in-tree DTS for the Miyoo Flip (rk3566-miyoo-355-v10-linux) was
designed for GammaOS Android. When used for Knulli (Linux), two issues
prevent display output:

1. chosen/bootargs contains "cma=0" which disables the Contiguous Memory
   Allocator. The Rockchip DRM driver requires CMA for framebuffer
   allocation. Without CMA, no display output is possible.

2. chosen/bootargs contains Android-specific parameters (androidboot.*,
   init=/init, mtdparts for SPI NAND) that are inappropriate for a Linux
   distribution booting from SD card.

Replace the Android bootargs with minimal Linux-appropriate ones that
preserve earlycon and console for debugging.

Signed-off-by: Alejandro Corbellini <acorbellini@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../dts/rockchip/rk3566-miyoo-355-v10-linux.dts   | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-miyoo-355-v10-linux.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-miyoo-355-v10-linux.dts
index 1111111111..2222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-miyoo-355-v10-linux.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-miyoo-355-v10-linux.dts
@@ -10,6 +10,6 @@

 	chosen {
-		bootargs = "console=tty0 console=ttyFIQ0 audit=0 firmware_class.path=/vendor/etc/firmware cma=0 init=/init rootwait ro loop.max_part=7 androidboot.console=ttyFIQ0 androidboot.hardware=rk30board androidboot.boot_devices=fe2b0000.dwmmc androidboot.selinux=permissive enforcing=0 mtdparts=spi-nand0:0x200000@0x000000(preloader),0x100000@0x200000(vnvm),0x400000@0x300000(uboot),0x2600000@0x700000(boot),0x4000000@0x2d00000(rootfs),0x1260000@0x6d00000(userdata)";
+		bootargs = "earlycon=uart8250,mmio32,0xfe660000 console=ttyFIQ0 console=tty0 rootwait";
 	};

 	gpio-keys {
--
2.43.0

